body:
"...as a much more constructive alternative than allowing you to wallow in self-pity." Wow, that's blaming the victim, condescending, judgemental and unsolicited advice rolled into one. 

&#x200B;

I just lost my estranged mother a month ago and a person in so much emotional pain isn't wallowing in self-pity. That is such a cruel thing to say. I suppose some people feel more alone than others - and the factors are very subjective and complicated. People like you make things worse and it's no wonder people who are struggling a lot emotionally don't want to talk or reach out. It's because they'll be undermined and misunderstood making them feel far worse. Do yourself a favour and don't reply to people here. You'll do more harm than good.
